# Line endings.
#
# Prettier is configured with its default `endOfLine: "lf"`, so a CRLF working
# copy makes `prettier --check` fail on files nobody has edited - the diff is
# invisible in a review and impossible to fix by editing. Normalising here is
# what lets formatting be a gate rather than permanent noise.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content and leave it alone; `eol=lf`
# pins the working-copy ending on every platform, so a Windows checkout and a
# Linux CI runner produce byte-identical files.
* text=auto eol=lf

